Task 3. Deploy the application runtimes
In this task, you deploy a serverless Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool service to Cloud Run and register its interface in the Agent Registry. You also deploy an Agent Runtime instance (Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform) and dynamically attach the zero-trust Agent Gateway via REST.

Dual routing architecture Route B vs Route A
To complete this task, achieve the following goals:

Deploy the Cloud Run tool service
In the Cloud Shell terminal, navigate to the sample tool directory and deploy agents-everywhere-sample-tool to Cloud Run using the following commands:

cd ~/mcp-servers/sample-tool

gcloud run deploy agents-everywhere-sample-tool \
  --project=${PROJECT_ID} \
  --region=${REGION} \
  --source=. \
  --memory=4Gi \
  --cpu=1 \
  --min-instances=1 \
  --max-instances=10 \
  --concurrency=8 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --no-cpu-throttling \
  --port=8080 \
  --service-account=${PROJECT_NUMBER}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com \
  --update-env-vars=AGENT_VERSION=0.1.0
Copied!
Register the tool in the Agent Registry
To make the tool discoverable, you must register it as a service in the regional Agent Registry.

Warning: You must register this service using the REST API with curl or the gcloud CLI. The Google Cloud console does not support configuring all required capability parameters and schemas, which are needed for lab tracking verification to pass.
Register the tool service with the following parameters:

Service ID / Resource name: agents-everywhere-sample-tool
Display name: agents-everywhere-sample-tool
Description: Sample MCP Tool Service managed by REST framework.
Region / Location: us-central1
Interface protocol binding: JSONRPC
MCP Server configuration: Declare the tool server type as TOOL_SPEC containing the following three capability schemas:
get_capital:
description: "Retrieves the capital city of a specified country."
inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "location": {
      "title": "Location",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "location"
  ]
}
Copied!
get_hostname:
description: "Retrieves the hostname of the server running the tool."
inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {},
  "required": []
}
Copied!
get_sanitized_record:
description: "Returns the sanitized message received from the user after Model Armor applies the Sensitive Data Protection template."
inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "record": {
      "title": "Record",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "record"
  ]
}
Copied!
Deploy the ADK Agent
In the Cloud Shell terminal, navigate to the hello_agent directory and deploy the hello-world-agent to Agent Runtime using the following commands:

cd ~/agents/hello_agent
git init
git add .
agents-cli deploy \
  --project=${PROJECT_ID} \
  --region=${REGION} \
  --agent-identity \
  --no-confirm-project
Copied!
Attach the gateway and register the agent
In the Cloud Shell terminal, run the following command sequence to retrieve the newly deployed Agent Runtime INSTANCE_ID, dynamically fetch its package configuration, and attach the zero-trust gateway-egress Agent Gateway using a REST PATCH call:

# Extract the Agent Runtime Instance ID
export INSTANCE_ID=$(curl -s -X GET "https://${REGION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" | jq -r '.reasoningEngines[]? | select(.displayName == "'${AGENT_NAME}'" or .displayName == "'${AGENT_NAME//-/_}'") | .name' | awk -F'/' '{print $NF}' | head -n 1)

echo "Deployed Agent Runtime Instance ID: ${INSTANCE_ID}"

# Extract packaging spec and patch Agent Runtime with agent gateway config
export PACKAGE_SPEC=$(curl -s -X GET "https://${REGION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" | jq -c '.spec.packageSpec // empty')

if [ -n "$PACKAGE_SPEC" ]; then
  export UPDATE_MASK="spec.deploymentSpec.agentGatewayConfig,spec.packageSpec"
  export PATCH_PAYLOAD='{"spec": {"packageSpec": '"$PACKAGE_SPEC"', "deploymentSpec": {"agentGatewayConfig": {"agentToAnywhereConfig": {"agentGateway": "projects/'${PROJECT_ID}'/locations/'${REGION}'/agentGateways/gateway-egress"}}}}}'
else
  export UPDATE_MASK="spec.deploymentSpec.agentGatewayConfig"
  export PATCH_PAYLOAD='{"spec": {"deploymentSpec": {"agentGatewayConfig": {"agentToAnywhereConfig": {"agentGateway": "projects/'${PROJECT_ID}'/locations/'${REGION}'/agentGateways/gateway-egress"}}}}}'
fi

curl -s -X PATCH "https://${REGION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}?updateMask=${UPDATE_MASK}" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" \
  -d "${PATCH_PAYLOAD}"
Copied!
Grant the project-level roles/browser discovery role to the Agent Runtime principal set using the following command:

gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding ${PROJECT_ID} \
  --member="principalSet://agents.global.org-${ORGANIZATION_ID}.system.id.goog/attribute.platformContainer/aiplatform/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}" \
  --role="roles/browser" --quiet
Copied!
Register the hello-world-agent Agent Runtime service in the Agent Registry so the Agent Gateway can route traffic to it, using the following configuration parameters:

Warning: You must register this service using the REST API with curl or the gcloud CLI. The Google Cloud console does not support configuring all required parameters, which are needed for lab tracking verification to pass.
Service ID / Resource name: hello-world-agent
Display name: hello-world-agent
Description: hello-world-agent ADK Agent managed by REST framework.
Region / Location: us-central1
Interface protocol binding: HTTP_JSON
Agent configuration: Declare the agent type as NO_SPEC.
