Task 4. Enforce the access control policies
In this task, you configure Identity-Aware Proxy (IAP) authorization policies on the target MCP server resources in the Agent Registry, forcing the Agent Gateway to verify native Workload Identity credentials before forwarding tool invocations.

Review the Terraform authorization configuration
Before applying changes, you should review how the authorization logic is defined in Terraform to see how security boundaries are managed.

Open terraform/gateway/main.tf in Cloud Shell to locate the google_network_services_authz_extension resource named iap_authz_extension:

# Create the Authz Service Extension for delegated verification
resource "google_network_services_authz_extension" "iap_authz_extension" {
  name              = "${var.agent_gateway_name}-iap-ext"
  location          = var.region
  service           = "iap.googleapis.com"
  timeout           = "3s"
  fail_open         = false
  forward_headers   = ["Authorization", "X-Goog-User-Project"]

  metadata = {
    iapPolicyVersion   = "V1"
    iamEnforcementMode = var.enable_iap_enforcement ? null : "DRY_RUN"
  }
}
Copied!
Review the metadata block configurations:

iamEnforcementMode: Configured dynamically. When enable_iap_enforcement is set to false, it defaults to "DRY_RUN". In dry-run mode, authorization policies are evaluated and logged but not actively blocked, which allows for initial testing.
When enable_iap_enforcement is toggled to true, the enforcement mode becomes active (null), instructing the load balancer to block any requests that are not fully authorized by IAP.
Locate the google_network_security_authz_policy resource named egress_authz_policy, which binds the authorization extension to your Agent Gateway to establish a centralized Zero-Trust Policy Enforcement Point (PEP) at the network edge.

Enforce the access control policies
In this section, you configure the required access control policies to establish zero-trust communication paths between your Agent Runtime agent and your Cloud Run tool service.

Configure the access policies by completing the following steps:

Grant invoker permissions on your agents-everywhere-sample-tool Cloud Run service to both your project's default compute service account (${PROJECT_NUMBER}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com) and your Agent Runtime workload identity (principal://agents.global.org-${ORGANIZATION_ID}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}).

Run the following commands in Cloud Shell to grant the invoker role:

gcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding agents-everywhere-sample-tool \
  --member="serviceAccount:${PROJECT_NUMBER}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/run.invoker" \
  --region=${REGION} \
  --project=${PROJECT_ID} --quiet

gcloud run services add-iam-policy-binding agents-everywhere-sample-tool \
  --member="principal://agents.global.org-${ORGANIZATION_ID}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}" \
  --role="roles/run.invoker" \
  --region=${REGION} \
  --project=${PROJECT_ID} --quiet
Copied!
Bind the Service Account Token Creator role (roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator) on your default Compute service account to your Agent Runtime workload identity to allow token impersonation fallback.

Run the following command in Cloud Shell to bind the token creator role:

gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding ${PROJECT_NUMBER}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com \
  --member="principal://agents.global.org-${ORGANIZATION_ID}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}" \
  --role="roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator" \
  --project=${PROJECT_ID} --quiet
Copied!
Retrieve the internal dynamic UUID of your registered agents-everywhere-sample-tool service from the Agent Registry using the following commands:

export MCP_SERVER_UUID=$(curl -s "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1alpha/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/services/agents-everywhere-sample-tool" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" | grep -o '"registryResource": "[^"]*' | cut -d'/' -f6)

echo "MCP Server UUID: $MCP_SERVER_UUID"
Copied!
Configure the IAP egress authorization policy on the registered MCP server resource, granting the roles/iap.egressor capability to your Agent Runtime workload identity.

Run the following REST API call in Cloud Shell to set the IAP authorization policy:

curl -s -X POST "https://iap.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/${REGION}/iap_web/agentRegistry/mcpServers/${MCP_SERVER_UUID}:setIamPolicy" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{
    \"policy\": {
      \"bindings\": [
        {
          \"role\": \"roles/iap.egressor\",
          \"members\": [
            \"principal://agents.global.org-${ORGANIZATION_ID}.system.id.goog/resources/aiplatform/projects/${PROJECT_NUMBER}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}\"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }"
Copied!
Apply your Terraform configuration, targeting the module.gateway specifically and setting enable_iap_enforcement to true to enable active edge blocking.

Run the following commands in Cloud Shell to apply the gateway module with IAP enforcement active:

cd ~/terraform

terraform apply -auto-approve -lock-timeout=600s \
  -var=project_id=${PROJECT_ID} \
  -var=project_number=${PROJECT_NUMBER} \
  -var=region=${REGION} \
  -var=organization_id=${ORGANIZATION_ID} \
  -var=enable_iap_enforcement=true \
  -var=agent_gateway_name=gateway-egress \
  -var=artifact_registry_repo=agent-repo \
  -var=vpc_network_name=governed-agent-vpc \
  -var=subnet_name=agent-private-subnet \
  -var=network_attachment_name=gateway-egress-na \
  -var=enable_model_armor=false \
  -var=model_armor_request_template_id=agw-request-template \
  -var=model_armor_response_template_id=agw-response-template \
  -var=model_armor_inspect_template_id=agw-ssn-inspect-template \
  -var=model_armor_deidentify_template_id=agw-ssn-redaction-template \
  -var=enable_vertex_ai_integration=true \
  -var=vertex_ai_inspect_only=false \
  -target=module.gateway
Copied!
