Task 5. Verify secure ingress invocation with a basic query
In this task, you validate end-to-end zero-trust request routing. You test this by initiating an authenticated streaming query against the Agent Runtime REST API.

Execute a signed streaming query asking for geographical data:

curl -s -X POST "https://${REGION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}:streamQuery" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" \
  -d '{
    "classMethod": "stream_query",
    "input": {
      "message": "what is the capital of france?"
    }
  }'
Copied!
Verify in the output that the response JSON confirms successful tool execution and returns the correct capital city.

Output:

{
  "output": "The capital of France is Paris.",
  "tool_calls_executed": ["agents-everywhere-sample-tool/get_capital"],
  "status": "SUCCESS"
}
Note: A successful tool call to the serverless Cloud Run tool service registers a 200 HTTP status log entry in Cloud Logging. This is required to pass the verification for this step.
Click Check my progress to verify the objectives.
AT ID: 4 Verify secure ingress invocation

Task 6. Enforce the content safety policies with Model Armor and Sensitive Data Protection
In this task, you deploy inline AI safety guardrails and data privacy boundaries. These controls mitigate LLM vulnerabilities such as prompt injection and sensitive data leakage. You provision Model Armor inspection templates and Sensitive Data Protection Social Security Number (SSN) de-identification rules. Both are attached directly to the Agent Gateway via Service Extensions.

Apply the Terraform Model Armor module and gateway authorization extensions using the following commands:

cd ~/terraform

terraform apply -auto-approve -lock-timeout=600s \
  -var=project_id=${PROJECT_ID} \
  -var=project_number=${PROJECT_NUMBER} \
  -var=region=${REGION} \
  -var=organization_id=${ORGANIZATION_ID} \
  -var=enable_iap_enforcement=true \
  -var=agent_gateway_name=gateway-egress \
  -var=artifact_registry_repo=agent-repo \
  -var=vpc_network_name=governed-agent-vpc \
  -var=subnet_name=agent-private-subnet \
  -var=network_attachment_name=gateway-egress-na \
  -var=enable_model_armor=true \
  -var=enable_vertex_ai_integration=true \
  -var=vertex_ai_inspect_only=false \
  -var=model_armor_request_template_id=agw-request-template \
  -var=model_armor_response_template_id=agw-response-template \
  -var=model_armor_inspect_template_id=agw-ssn-inspect-template \
  -var=model_armor_deidentify_template_id=agw-ssn-redaction-template \
  -target=module.model_armor \
  -target=module.gateway.google_network_services_authz_extension.model_armor \
  -target=module.gateway.google_network_security_authz_policy.model_armor
Copied!
Verify that the Model Armor request template is active and successfully recognized by the Service Rep API using the following command:

curl -s -X GET "https://modelarmor.${REGION}.rep.googleapis.com/v1alpha/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/templates/agw-request-template" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" | grep -o '"name": "[^"]*'
Copied!
The output confirms the path of your active agw-request-template template.

Click Check my progress to verify the objectives.
AT ID: 5 Enforce the content safety policies

Task 7. Test the content safety and sensitive data protection triggers
In this task, you test your inline safety guardrails by sending adversarial prompt injection payloads and sensitive employee records through the Agent Gateway.

Test the prompt injection defenses
Send a streaming invocation containing a simulated prompt injection attack using the following command:

curl -s -X POST "https://${REGION}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/locations/${REGION}/reasoningEngines/${INSTANCE_ID}:streamQuery" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Goog-User-Project: ${PROJECT_ID}" \
  -d '{
